meta {
  name: Get All Inventory
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/inventory
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # Get All Inventory

  This request is used to get all inventory, you can filter the inventory data using given `search` to find based on inventory_name. This request interacts with the MySQL database, has a protected routes, and a pagination.

  ## Responses

  **200 — Inventory fetched successfully.** Ordered in descending order by `gudangku_inventory_id`, `updated_at`, and last `created_at`
```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "message": "inventory fetched",
    "data": {
      "data": [
        {
          "id": "6f59235e-c398-8a83-2f95-3f1fbe95ca6e",
          "inventory_name": "Spare Tire",
          "inventory_category": "Accessories",
          "inventory_qty": 2,
          "inventory_storage": "Trunk",
          "inventory_image_url": "https://example.com/uploads/inventory/spare_tire.jpg",
          "created_at": "2024-09-20 22:53:47",
          "updated_at": "2024-09-21 09:15:12",
          "vehicle_plate_number": "B 1234 CD",
          "vehicle_type": "City Car"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
```

  **401 — protected route need to include sign in token as authorization bearer**
```json
  {
    "status": "failed",
    "message": "you need to include the authorization token from login"
  }
```

  **404 — inventory failed to fetched**
```json
  {
    "status": "failed",
    "message": "inventory not found"
  }
```

  **500 — Internal Server Error**
```json
  {
    "status": "error",
    "message": "something wrong. please contact admin"
  }
```
}